	(text "Notes:\n- TX/RX are BOARD-side names: the pin named TX carries the board's UART*_TX net.\n  Check against the mark1 cables before crimping.\n- J3 (CON-1) and J5 (CON-3) are the same part; J5 may be DNP (SRC-3) until a real\n  radio arrives.\n- J4 (CON-2) pin order was chosen at schematic time - the spec does NOT freeze it.\n  Freeze this table before making the cable. The I2C1 pull-ups live on the Sensors\n  sheet, so there are none here.\n- J6 (ESC-3) is the BOARD'S MAIN POWER INPUT on pin 2 (+12V, PWR-1). The pinout is\n  frozen by the spec; verify the actual 4-in-1 harness wire order against this table\n  before crimping the cable.\n- J6 pin 7 CURR is the analog current-sense fallback (PWR-4 / SRC-3); pin 8 TLM is the\n  ESC telemetry UART RX (ESC-2). USART2_TX has no connector pin, only the TP5 pad.\n- Connectors sit on the board edges with the openings outward, side entry (MEC-2).\n- All hierarchical nets leave this sheet to the MCU sheet; nothing is wired between\n  sheet blocks in the root."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 130.81 158.75 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "289820ca-80f8-4b66-9b9a-16b630046e45")
	)
	(text "J4 - CON-2 GPS / external mag: 1 GND, 2 +3V3, 3 TX, 4 RX, 5 SCL, 6 SDA"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 76.2 105.41 0)
		(effects
